WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.253 --> 00:00:03.469
-Republican leaders have
announced their opposition

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:04.637
to a commission to investigate

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.872
the January 6th insurrection
at the Capitol

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:08.775
as the GOP
intensifies its efforts

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.209
to rewrite the history
of what happened.

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:12.845
For more on this, it's time
for A Closer Look.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:16.616
♪♪

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.618
Many Republican officials
have been desperate

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.053
to create
an alternate universe

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:22.488
where Donald Trump
is a beloved former president

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:23.889
who people miss and want back,

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:25.491
which is insane
for many reasons.

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:28.628
For one, everyone's
daily quality of life is better

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.396
without having to wake up
in the morning

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.398
to 10 different news alerts
on your phone

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:34.400
that all say something
along the lines of,

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.103
"President Trump accuses
Eiffel Tower of spying on him,

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.839
suggests eating a golf ball
can cure coronavirus."

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.475
The other reason
it's absurd is the fact

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.344
that Trump is our most
unpopular president

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.779
in the history
of modern polling.

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:48.748
He never won the popular vote,
lost by 7 million votes in 2020,

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.750
never once cracked
50% job approval,

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.620
and now spends his time
barging into weddings

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.855
to rant about voter fraud.

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:58.023
It's the most embarrassing thing

00:00:58.023 --> 00:00:59.592
that could possibly happen
at a wedding,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.128
aside from your mom
making you slow dance with her

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.262
while you're 13.

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:04.998
[ As teenage boy ] "Mom,
you're embarrassing me."

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.432
[ As mother ]
"Honey, fix your tie."

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:08.201
"I don't want to wear
the stupid bow tie.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.436
I wanted to wear
my tuxedo shirt."

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:13.372
"Well, your father and I
outvoted you two-to-one."

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:15.641
"There was voter fraud.

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:18.844
My friend Mike's dad
hanging out with Hugo Chavez."

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:19.946
"Which friend Mike?"

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.047
[ As Mike Lindell ]
"That would be me.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.016
Now, I know it might be weird

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:26.619
that I'm pals with
a 13-year-old,

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:30.823
but in my defense,
everything about me is weird."

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:32.292
Last night on Fox,
for example,

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.894
Trump's son Eric told
a ludicrous story

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.262
about how random people

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.264
are supposedly coming up
to him on the street

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.432
and telling him how much
they miss his father.

00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:42.735
-More people have come up to me
on the street in the last week

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:45.771
and given me hugs, saying,
"We miss him so much."

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:47.907
I mean, literally, sometimes,
Sean, with tears in their eyes.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.676
"We miss the man so much."

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.343
-Well, it's allergy season.

00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:52.812
Everybody has tears
in their eyes.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.614
Guy came up to me yesterday with
tears running down his face,

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:59.419
sniffling, and said,
"Hey, your show stinks."

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:02.989
Also, based on that story,
when you live in New York City,

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:06.158
you got to watch out
for the Impractical Jokers.

00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:09.395
I'm pretty sure "hug Eric Trump"
was Murr's punishment

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.131
last season for losing
the grocery store challenge.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:15.468
"Now, tell him you miss
his dad so much."

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:16.735
Second, it's nice to see

00:02:16.735 --> 00:02:18.538
Eric has inherited
his father's penchant

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:21.107
for inventing anonymous adults
who cry with gratitude.

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:24.144
I guess when you come from a
family devoid of human emotion,

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.978
it makes sense
that you would project it

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:27.346
onto imaginary friends.

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:29.482
[ As Eric ] "And Sean, this man,
still crying, said to me,

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:32.285
'Also, you're a good boy
and your daddy is proud of you,'

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.486
which I thought was
very nice of him to add."

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:37.490
Republicans have also been busy
trying to rewrite the history

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.326
of what happened
at the Capitol on January 6th.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.628
That's why GOP leaders
like Kevin McCarthy

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:44.730
and Mitch McConnell
have come out against creating

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.299
an independent commission
to investigate it.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.534
Many Republicans have
straight up lied about it,

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.936
which is hard to swallow,
because we all,

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:54.440
every one of us, saw it happen
in real time with our own eyes.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.744
Most of the people doing it
were also filming it.

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:59.812
It was one of those collective
national moments

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.914
where we were all watching
the same thing unfold

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:03.082
together in shock,

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.851
like the O.J. trial
or the Apollo 13 landing,

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:09.688
or David Copperfield making
the Statue of Liberty disappear.

00:03:09.688 --> 00:03:11.324
And by the way, if you've
never been to New York,

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:14.160
you might not know this --
he never put it back.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.296
All we have is
a cheap cardboard cutout.

00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:19.999
Anyway, the point is, we all saw
the Capitol riot happen,

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.333
and if by some chance
you weren't

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:22.635
glued to your TV that day,

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.971
there are plenty of first-person
accounts you can watch

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.405
from reporters who were there,

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:28.741
documenting the violence
as it was happening.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:31.578
-The pro-Trump crowd
fought with the police,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.584
trying to break
through their lines,

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:39.818
intoxicated by
the unlikely prospect

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:42.121
of reversing
America's election outcome.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.790
This is exactly
what was feared,

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.993
but in no way
is this a surprise.

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:50.129
It has being fueled
by the president's rhetoric.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:53.532
We followed the aggrieved
and infuriated Trump supporters

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:55.568
as they stormed the building.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:59.738
-I swear that's CNN.

00:03:59.738 --> 00:04:04.243
-Through broken windows
and doors they had forced open,

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:07.413
the cost of that rhetoric
is increasingly clear.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.715
-I know my rights!

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:13.352
-As crowds tonight are still
swirling around Congress...

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:17.456
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:20.626
...and America's long journey
as a stable democracy

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:23.095
appears to be in genuine doubt.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.397
-It's always sobering to watch
a British correspondent

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:26.833
report on American chaos.

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.167
[ In British accent ]
"Rioters have now

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.870
breached the capitol of
this once-proud democracy,

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.340
and like an Earl Gray tea bag
on a porcelain sink,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.909
it will leave
an indelible stain.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:41.547
Now stay tuned for yet
another rerun of 'Taskmasters.'"

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.383
Somehow, the reverse
is never as harrowing.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:44.717
Even when Brexit was a mess

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.352
and the government
there was in crisis,

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.187
it just wasn't
as dramatic to listen

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.022
to an American report on it.

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:52.058
"Yeah, Cliff, things are not
going well over here

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:53.792
with all this Brexit stuff.

00:04:53.792 --> 00:04:57.530
It's a...it's a real...
It's real mess.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.232
Is there a hurricane
I can report on?

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:01.100
Because this [bleep]
is complicated."

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.970
It's the same as watching one of
those BBC Nature documentaries.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.938
The British accents
really hit home

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:06.972
how dramatic it is.

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:08.607
It would be a lot
less compelling

00:05:08.607 --> 00:05:10.075
with an American narrator.

00:05:10.075 --> 00:05:11.510
"And the iguana is like,

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.513
'Alright, I'm just
gonna stay still

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.448
and that snake's
not gonna see me.

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:17.983
Just stay still. Stay still.

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:20.619
Oh, no! It saw me!
I'm gonna run crazy!

00:05:20.619 --> 00:05:23.589
I'm going to do my crazy run.
Oh, there are so many snakes.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.824
I think maybe right now I'm
gonna just go to the rocks.

00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:28.227
The rocks will be
a safe place for me.

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:30.563
Oh, no, they live there!
This is their house.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:34.300
And now I'm going to, I don't
know, activate my iguana oil.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.501
Is that a thing?

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.269
And I'm gonna slip out
and now I'm gonna jump

00:05:37.269 --> 00:05:39.405
like I'm on a trampoline
up this mountain.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.874
Boing, boing.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.208
And now the snake's like,
I got you.

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:45.144
And then he's gonna follow me
like, I don't have hands.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.179
And now this iguana
is finally up here

00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:49.882
and his friend is gonna
be like, 'Where were you?'

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:58.224
And it's like, 'Where was I?
How about, how am I?'"

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:00.726
Not as good.

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:03.262
But it's all there on camera
for us to see,

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:06.799
and yet Republicans are engaged
in an intensifying effort

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:08.301
to rewrite
the history of that day

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:10.235
by claiming, preposterously,

00:06:10.235 --> 00:06:12.137
that the entire thing
was a peaceful protest.

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:13.639
-Let me be clear.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.342
There was no insurrection,
and to call it an insurrection,

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:19.077
in my opinion,
is a bold-faced lie.

00:06:19.077 --> 00:06:21.881
Watching the TV footage of those
who entered the Capitol

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.850
and walked through Statuary Hall

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.618
showed people
in an orderly fashion

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.386
staying between
the stanchions and robes,

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.155
taking videos and pictures.

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.956
You know, if you didn't know
the TV footage

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:33.358
was a video
from January the 6th,

00:06:33.358 --> 00:06:36.195
you would actually think it was
a normal tourist visit.

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:39.699
-This didn't seem like
an armed insurrection to me.

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:41.000
I mean, "armed."

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.669
When you hear "armed,"
don't you think of firearms?

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:48.541
-There's no evidence, as has
been said on January 7th,

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:51.611
that this was
an armed insurrection.

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:55.080
There have been things
worse than people

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:59.352
without any firearms
coming into a building.

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:01.086
-Okay, first of all,
describing it as

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:03.289
"people without firearms
coming into a building"

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:05.557
leaves out a lot
of crucial context.

00:07:05.557 --> 00:07:08.060
It's like writing a book report
about "The Great Gatsby"

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.429
that says, "Man enjoys summer
in the Hamptons."

00:07:10.429 --> 00:07:11.830
Also, it's a lie.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.433
There were weapons,
as the Justice Department,

00:07:14.433 --> 00:07:16.535
reporters, and video
have all documented.

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:19.938
But even if that statement were
true, it's not very comforting.

00:07:19.938 --> 00:07:21.707
If a group of criminals
breaks into your house

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.075
with some baseball bat,

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:25.410
smashes all your belongings,
and steals all your money,

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:26.511
it wouldn't exactly
make you feel better

00:07:26.511 --> 00:07:27.613
if the cops were like,

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:29.348
"Hey, there are
worse things in life.

00:07:29.348 --> 00:07:32.250
Eric Trump's out there just
hugging people in the street."

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.253
Second, peaceful tour groups
don't usually have

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:35.988
British correspondents
following them around

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:38.123
as they smash barricades,
break windows,

00:07:38.123 --> 00:07:40.626
attack police officers,
and vandalize offices.

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:43.129
If it really was
a normal tourist visit,

00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:44.931
that report would have been
a lot less dramatic.

00:07:44.931 --> 00:07:46.832
[ In British accent ] "The group
is now moving down the hallway

00:07:46.832 --> 00:07:48.867
into the rotunda as
the tour guide provides

00:07:48.867 --> 00:07:52.638
a substantive history
of neoclassical architecture.

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.540
Several people are looking down
at their phones,

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.741
and one man seems to be --

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.444
yes, I can confirm
he is falling asleep.

00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:02.348
Now, stay tuned for
an all-new 'Mock the Week.'"

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:04.650
I also want to draw attention to

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.420
this part of
Senator Ron Johnson's argument.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.488
-If that was a planned
armed insurrection,

00:08:09.488 --> 00:08:12.024
man, you have really
a bunch of idiots.

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:15.794
-Here's an idea --
maybe both are true.

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:17.896
Stupid people also make plans.

00:08:17.896 --> 00:08:20.699
Have you ever seen an empty
Dave &amp; Buster's?

00:08:20.699 --> 00:08:22.534
Maybe it was
a planned insurrection

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:24.036
and they were idiots.

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:26.204
I mean, one dude was
dressed like a [bleep] Viking.

00:08:26.204 --> 00:08:28.774
If he barged into my house,
I'd still be terrified.

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:30.876
If somebody barged into my house
dressed like Tom Hanks,

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:34.046
I'd be terrified,
and everyone loves Tom Hanks.

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:36.548
I wouldn't be like, "Oh, I'm
sure this Hanks enthusiast

00:08:36.548 --> 00:08:38.884
is in my house for good stuff."

00:08:38.884 --> 00:08:40.987
This is why we need a commission
to lay out the facts

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:42.588
as we know them
for the historical record,

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:44.256
so Republicans
can't lie about it

00:08:44.256 --> 00:08:46.792
and create an alternate reality
where it didn't happen.

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:49.161
If there isn't an accurate
historical account

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:51.497
of the insurrection
with shame and consequences

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:54.166
for the people involved,
it could very well happen again.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.768
Republicans would rather
not talk about

00:08:55.768 --> 00:08:57.970
the consequences of their
actions, so they're whining.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.306
-Literally, sometimes, Sean,
with tears in their eyes.

00:09:00.306 --> 00:09:02.308
-This has been A Closer Look.

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:05.844
♪♪

